#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# erf

#% text
# `erf(x)` gives the error function of `x`, `2/sqrt(pi)` times the integral of `exp(-t^2)` for `t` from 0 to `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 7.2.1. `erf` is odd, and tends to 1 as `x` tends to `inf`.

#% item
# `erf(0)` is 0; other exact arguments stay unevaluated. Use `n` for a numerical value.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex machine numbers give numerical values.

#% item
# Close to 1, the difference `1 - erf(x)` loses all digits; use `erfc(x)`, which stays accurate deep in the tail.

#% item
# `erf` is listable: it applies to each element of a list.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
erf(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.8427007929497149

#% cell
erf(-1.0)
#% output
#= -0.8427007929497149

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(erf(1), 30)
#% output
#= 0.8427007929497148693412206350826093

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A ball:

#% cell
erf(1/2~30)
#% output
#= 0.52049987781304653768274665389

#% text
# A complex machine number:

#% cell
erf(1.0 + 1.0*im)
#% output
#= 1.3161512816979477 + 0.19045346923783468im

#% text
# Each element of a list:

#% cell
erf([0.0, 0.5, 1.0])
#% output
#= [0.0, 0.5204998778130465, 0.8427007929497149]

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The probability that a normal random value lies within one standard deviation of its mean:

#% cell
erf(1/sqrt(2.0))
#% output
#= 0.6826894921370859

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The derivative is a Gaussian:

#% cell
d(erf(x), x)
#% output
#= 2*exp(-x^2)/pi^(1/2)

#% text
# The integral of the Gaussian gives the same value:

#% cell
n_integrate(2/sqrt(pi)*exp(-t^2), [t, 0, 1])
#% output
#= 0.842700792949715

#% text
# `erfc` is the complement:

#% cell
erf(0.3) + erfc(0.3)
#% output
#= 1.0

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Far in the tail, `1 - erf(x)` is 0 in machine numbers; `erfc` keeps the value:

#% cell
1 - erf(6.0)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% cell
erfc(6.0)
#% output
#= 2.1519736712498913e-17


#% text
# An odd function:

#% cell
erf(-a)
#% output
#= -erf(a)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `erfc`, `erfi`, `inverse_erfc`, `normal_distribution`, `gamma`
